From: Protium
Subject: [PATCH] wsi/metal: Keep three drawables when an application asks for two images

The surface reports minImageCount 3, but the swapchain takes the
application's count as it is, and DOOM (2016) asks for 2: its CAMetalLayer
then has two drawables, one always on screen. vkAcquireNextImageKHR waits in
nextDrawable until the frame just presented has been drawn and shown, so
drawing and showing run one after the other. With FIFO that does not stay at
a refresh or two of delay: while the game waits the GPU has nothing to do
and slows down, its frames take longer and miss more refreshes, and it slows
down more, and looks busy enough all the while.

DOOM in a fight at 2560x1440 on a 120 Hz screen (M4 Pro), FIFO, from the
driver's own lines (KK_PRESENT_STATS=30), half minutes of two sessions the
same afternoon:

                          2 drawables       3 drawables
  frames a second         24 to 26          75 to 102
  GPU time a frame        33 to 35 ms       9.3 to 11.5 ms
  GPU busy                84 to 88%         87 to 99%
  wait in acquire         31 to 38 ms       0.1 to 1.8 ms
  present to the screen   46 to 48 ms       23 to 27 ms

Before the fight, with two drawables: 60 fps and 9.8 ms of GPU time a frame
at 59% busy. The two-drawable session stayed at 24 to 26 fps for five half
minutes on end; the three-drawable one had no such stretch in seven minutes.

Give the layer three drawables in that case. The application's images are
blit sources bound to whichever drawable comes next, so it still sees the two
it asked for.

